course: dictionary
lesson: 2735
title: Directly: straight, exact, or at once
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Directly is a small word with a big job. It can mean going straight to a place, with nothing turning off on the way. «Come directly home after school» means go home without stopping anywhere else.
explain: Directly can also mean exactly. If a map shows the shop directly opposite the school, the shop is right across the road in that exact spot, not somewhere nearby.
explain: Directly can mean with nothing in between, like «talk directly to someone». Ask yourself: is anything or anyone standing between them? If not, directly is the right meaning.
explain: Directly can also mean immediately, or very soon, but this meaning is mainly British and a bit old-fashioned. Check the context: if the sentence is about where something is, or how someone is linked to something, it probably does not mean this.
fact: Directly means straight, exact, or with nothing in between.
fact: «Directly above» means right above, with nothing to the side.
fact: «Directly opposite» means exactly across from something.
fact: «Good doctors talk to children directly, because children often know best how they feel.» Here directly means with nothing in between: the doctor speaks to the child, not only to the parent.
fact: Never look directly at the Sun; it can damage your eyes.
exercise: «Come directly home after school.» What does directly mean here? | Slowly and carefully | *Without stopping anywhere else | With a friend | Late at night
exercise: «The shop is directly opposite the school.» What does directly show? | *Right across from it, in exactly that spot | Somewhere down the road | Inside the school
exercise: «Never look directly at the Sun.» Why is this a safety rule? | *It can damage your eyes | It is too warm to touch
test: «Good doctors talk to children directly.» What does directly mean? | Through a letter | Very quickly, at once | Only sometimes | *With nothing in between, straight to the child
test: «The bench is directly below the tree.» What does directly show? | *Exact position, with nothing to the side | How long the tree has been there | A feeling of sadness | Speed
exam: Which sentence uses directly to mean going straight to a place? | It rained a lot last week | The cat slept under the bed | Lots of children laughed at the joke | *«Go directly to the library after lunch.»
